Web Server, Wi-Fi and JSON API

Current prototype networking:
#include <WiFi.h>
#include <WebServer.h>

Server:
WebServer server(80)

Required routes:
GET /          → Dashboard
GET /data      → JSON measurement API
GET /downloadcsv → CSV download

JSON example:
{
  "freq1": 10.0000,
  "freq2": 9.9000,
  "freq3": 9.8000,
  "freq4": 8.7000
}

The API returns the latest calculated values and must not initiate a new measurement.

Wi-Fi:
Use station mode.
Credentials in the public GitHub source must be placeholders:
const char* WIFI_SSID = "YOUR_SSID";
const char* WIFI_PASSWORD = "YOUR_PASSWORD";

Never commit real Wi-Fi credentials.

NTP:
Server: pool.ntp.org
India offset: 19800 seconds
Daylight offset: 0

The firmware shall print Wi-Fi status, IP address and NTP synchronization status to Serial.

